% WIDEN: ADD A DEMAND-ZERO SECTION OF 200 PAGES TO AN EXE MADE BY IMAGE,
% AFTER ITS FIXUP-VECTOR ISD AND BEFORE THE SHAREABLE IMAGES.  IT GOES AT
% 40000, OR ON THE PAGE AFTER THE FIXUP VECTOR IF THE EXE REACHES PAST
% 40000 (PHASE 7'S DOES).  THE EXE THEN RUNS WITH P0 ENDING 40000 HIGHER
% THAN WHERE IT WAS MADE: ITS SHAREABLES, AND EVERY REGION THE KERNEL
% $EXPREGS, LAND HIGHER, AS ON A SYSTEM WITH LARGER SHAREABLES.  NEEDS
% HEAD AND IMAGE_FRAB, IMAGE'S WORDS IN IORB<, SO A PATCHED STOIC.EXE
% (DEFECT 22).  IT USES BLOCK I/O: AN EXE
% MADE BY IMAGE HAS VARIABLE-LENGTH RECORDS, SO A KEYED GET OR PUT (AS IN
% IMAGE'S FRANDOPUT AND NOCREF) GIVES RMS-F-RAC.
%   'FILE WIDEN
HEX
IORB<
0 'WAT VARIABLE  0 'WN VARIABLE  0 'WV VARIABLE
'WIDEN :
  INIT_FRABS IMAGE_FRAB CUR_FRAB !
  DUP COUNT FAB.M_GET FAB.M_BIO OR FOPEN SYSERR
  HEAD 200 FREAD SYSERR  FCLOSE SYSERR  % VBN 1, THE HEADER
  HEAD DUP W@ +
  BEGIN DUP 8 + @ 400 AND EQZ IF DUP W@ + REPEAT  % TO THE FIXUP ISD
  DUP 4+ @ FFFFFF AND OVER 2+ W@ + 200 MAX WV !  % THE NEW SECTION'S VPN
  DUP W@ + DUP WAT !  % THE NEW ISD GOES AFTER IT
  BEGIN DUP W@ NEZ IF DUP W@ + REPEAT 2+  % END OF THE LIST
  WAT @ - WN !
  WN @ 0 DO WAT @ I + B@ BLOCKBUF I + B! LOOP
  WN @ 0 DO BLOCKBUF I + B@ WAT @ C + I + B! LOOP
  C WAT @ W!  200 WAT @ 2+ W!  WV @ WAT @ 4+ !  8C WAT @ 8 + !
  COUNT FAB.M_PUT FAB.M_BIO OR FOPEN SYSERR
  HEAD 200 FWRITE SYSERR  FCLOSE SYSERR ;  % WRITE IT BACK
>
DECIMAL
